<section id="lanes" class="feature" aria-labelledby="lanes-title">
  <div class="section-heading copy">
    <h2 id="lanes-title">Run several copies of your project</h2>
    <p>
      A lane groups the services and configuration for one running stack. Use separate worktrees,
      another checkout, or the same checkout with different settings.
    </p>
  </div>
  <div class="lane-details">
    <article class="copy">
      <h3>Ports and hostnames</h3>
      <p>
        Each lane gets a port range and local hostnames. Run the checkout branch alongside main
        without assigning ports in <code>.env</code> files.
      </p>
      <code class="example">
        main :20000
        <br />
        checkout :21000
      </code>
    </article>
    <article class="copy">
      <h3>Per-lane databases</h3>
      <p>
        Lanes can share a Postgres server while using separate databases. Test a migration in one
        lane without changing main's data.
      </p>
      <code class="example">
        postgres / myapp_main
        <br />
        postgres / myapp_lane1
      </code>
    </article>
    <article class="copy">
      <h3>Project configuration</h3>
      <p>
        Define services and setup tasks in <code>devlanes.yaml</code>. Environment variables use
        each lane's ports and database names.
      </p>
      <code class="example">
        devlanes.yaml
        <br />
        web + api + worker
      </code>
    </article>
  </div>
</section>
